{"title":"Career Roadmap · Tissue Engineer","role":"Tissue Engineer","summary":"A Tissue Engineer applies engineering, biology, materials science, and biotechnology to develop biological substitutes or systems that can repair, regenerate, or replace damaged tissues.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. — Engineering & Technology","Course":"Biomanufacturing / Bioengineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Tissue Engineer applies engineering, biology, materials science, and biotechnology to develop biological substitutes or systems that can repair, regenerate, or replace damaged tissues."},{"type":"p","text":"The field combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Biomaterials"},{"text":"Biomedical engineering"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Biofabrication"},{"text":"3D bioprinting"},{"text":"Tissue culture"},{"text":"Regenerative medicine"},{"text":"Microfluidics"},{"text":"Computational modeling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing tissue-engineering scaffolds"},{"text":"Culturing and studying cells"},{"text":"Developing biomaterials"},{"text":"Supporting tissue regeneration experiments"},{"text":"Developing 3D-bioprinted tissue constructs"},{"text":"Characterizing engineered tissues"},{"text":"Performing laboratory experiments"},{"text":"Analyzing biological and engineering data"},{"text":"Supporting preclinical research"},{"text":"Working with interdisciplinary research teams"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important career note","text":"A B.Tech can provide a strong foundation, but many dedicated tissue-engineering R&D and research positions expect an M.Tech/MS/PhD or substantial laboratory research experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Biomedical / Tissue Engineering Intern","Research Assistant / Junior Tissue Engi