"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biological signals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Growth factors"},{"text":"Cytokines"},{"text":"Cell signaling"},{"text":"Mechanical stimulation"},{"text":"Biochemical cues"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Scaffold Design & Biomaterials"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn scaffold fabrication methods:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Electrospinning"},{"text":"Freeze-drying"},{"text":"Solvent-based methods"},{"text":"Hydrogel fabrication"},{"text":"Decellularization concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scaffold requirements"},{"type":"p","text":"A good scaffold may need:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biocompatibility"},{"text":"Appropriate mechanical properties"},{"text":"Controlled degradation"},{"text":"Suitable porosity"},{"text":"Cell attachment"},{"text":"Nutrient transport"},{"text":"Tissue-specific architecture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — 3D Bioprinting"},{"type":"p","text":"3D bioprinting is a major emerging area."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bioinks"},{"text":"Extrusion bioprinting"},{"text":"Inkjet bioprinting concepts"},{"text":"Bioprinting parameters"},{"text":"Crosslinking"},{"text":"Cell viability"},{"text":"Layer-by-layer fabrication"},{"text":"Scaffold architecture"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pipeline:"},{"type":"flow","items":["3D Tissue Model","CAD Design","Bioink Selection","Bioprinting","Crosslinking","Cell Culture","Tissue Maturation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Bioreactors"},{"type":"p","text":"Tissue constructs often require controlled environments."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bioreactor principles"},{"text":"Oxygen transport"},{"text":"Nutrient transport"},{"text":"Fluid flow"},{"text":"Shear stress"},{"text":"Mechanical stimulation"},{"text":"Temperature/pH control"},{"text":"Perfusion systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Architecture:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Bioreactor","Controlled Envi